```java
// ✅ ArrayDeque (Double-Ended Queue)
ArrayDeque<String> deque = new ArrayDeque<>();
deque.add("A");          // add at tail
deque.addFirst("B");     // add at head
deque.addLast("C");      // add at tail
deque.removeFirst();     // remove from head
deque.removeLast();      // remove from tail
// Tip: Use ArrayDeque as a faster stack or queue alternative (no null elements allowed).

// ✅ Set (Unique Collection)
Set<String> set = new HashSet<>();
set.add("apple");
set.add("banana");
set.add("apple"); // duplicate ignored
set.contains("banana");  // true
set.remove("apple");     // removes element
// Tip: Set stores unique elements only — ideal for avoiding duplicates.
```

